'/how-it-works':{title:'How Preflight works',intro:'A static review workflow with explicit evidence boundaries.',sections:[['Choose the inputs','Connect a public repository and select baseline/proposed refs, upload ZIP source archives, or supply two OpenAPI JSON specifications.'],['Run the supported checks','The worker inspects supported source and contract structures without executing customer code. Inputs that exceed limits or cannot be analyzed are reported or rejected.'],['Review the evidence','Inspect each finding’s rule, location, confidence, and recommended action. A completed scan is not a passing deployment test.'],['Validate before release','Use findings to guide your own tests and review. Download the evidence and follow your normal deployment approval process.']]},
